    summary_en: "The case involves former ransomware negotiator Angelo Martino, who was accused of colluding with the now-defunct BlackCat ransomware operators to extort victims using their sensitive information. Martino had represented five different ransomware victims in negotiations, but leaked confidential information—such as victims' insurance policy limits and internal negotiation positions—to the BlackCat attackers. This information allowed the attackers to maximize the ransom amount. Furthermore, Martino, along with two other professionals (Ryan Goldberg and Kevin Martin), assisted in deploying BlackCat ransomware attacks against multiple U.S. victims in 2023. The U.S. Department of Justice noted that the case revealed how insiders betray victims by providing their confidential negotiation information to criminal groups, thereby exacerbating the victims' losses. Law enforcement seized Martino's assets, including digital currency and multiple vehicles. This case serves as a warning about the moral risks and the severity of information leakage by insiders during cyber incidents.",
