    id: "20260710-040",
    trackers: ["security"],
    category: "供應鏈與開源安全",
    title: "電信巨頭Lumen揭露資產盲點：從1.7萬至110萬資產，凸顯企業資產盤點的重大風險",
    summary: "本報導引用Axonius的報告，指出許多企業的資產盤點往往存在嚴重偏差。電信公司Lumen Technologies的案例展示了這一問題：他們最初僅掌握約1.7萬個已知資產，但透過Axonius資產情報平台整合超過40個分散系統的數據後，實際範圍擴大至約110萬個設備。這凸顯了傳統資安工具無法提供統一、準確的資產全貌。\n\n在資產盤點不精確的情況下，企業在應對零日漏洞時，難以快速確定受影響系統、所有權和外部暴露狀態。Lumen利用整合的資產數據，成功建立了應用層級的風險評估儀表板，將資安風險與業務營收掛鉤。這使得安全團隊能從傳統的「掃描與垃圾訊息」（scan and spam）模式，轉向更智能的、基於風險的暴露管理，實現更精準的修補優先級排序。最終，精準的資產數據使Lumen的領導層決策得以升級，促使其進行大規模雲端遷移，並大幅提升了資安投資。",
    tags: ["Lumen Technologies", "資產盤點", "Axonius", "暴露管理", "資安風險", "CMDB"],
    title_en: "Telecom Giant Lumen Reveals Asset Blind Spots: From 17K to 1.1M Assets, Highlighting Major Enterprise Asset Inventory Risks",
    summary_en: "This report cites a report by Axonius, pointing out that many enterprises' asset inventories often contain significant deviations. The case of telecommunications company Lumen Technologies demonstrates this issue: they initially only accounted for approximately 17,000 known assets, but after integrating data from over 40 disparate systems using the Axonius asset intelligence platform, the actual scope expanded to approximately 1.1 million devices. This highlights that traditional security tools cannot provide a unified and accurate view of all assets. When asset inventory is inaccurate, enterprises struggle to quickly determine affected systems, ownership, and external exposure when responding to zero-day vulnerabilities. Lumen utilized the integrated asset data to successfully build an application-level risk assessment dashboard, linking security risks directly to business revenue. This allowed the security team to shift from a traditional 'scan and spam' model to a smarter, risk-based exposure management approach, achieving more precise patching prioritization. Ultimately, accurate asset data elevated Lumen's executive decision-making, prompting a large-scale cloud migration and significantly increasing security investments.",
    tags_en: ["Lumen Technologies", "Asset Inventory", "Axonius", "Exposure Management", "Security Risk", "CMDB"],
