    summary_en: "Apple has filed a lawsuit against OpenAI, accusing the company and its former employees of stealing Apple's trade secrets and non-public technical information. The lawsuit alleges that former employees, such as Tang Tan (former Apple VP of Product Design) and Chang Liu (former Senior Systems Electrical Engineer), used internal knowledge to obtain details of confidential Apple projects during interviews, and even instructed current Apple employees to bring in physical hardware components and prototypes for 'demonstration.' Apple further accuses former employee Liu of downloading technical documents containing complex circuit board manufacturing details using security vulnerabilities after leaving the company, and failing to return company equipment. Apple emphasizes that this improper conduct has become a 'pattern,' and that it had warned OpenAI, which received no response. Apple's lawsuit aims to prevent the outflow of this confidential information and protect its core technology and intellectual property.",
