    title: "警惕 Joomla 關鍵漏洞：SP Page Builder 與 Page Builder CK 遭積極利用，建議立即修補",
    summary: "內容管理系統 Joomla 的擴充套件存在兩項關鍵漏洞，目前據報已遭積極利用。受影響的漏洞包括 CVE-2026-48908（影響 SP Page Builder 擴充套件，適用於 Joomla 6.6.2 之前版本）和 CVE-2026-56290（影響 Page Builder CK 擴充套件，適用於 Joomla 3.6.0 之前版本）。這兩漏洞的 CVSS v3.1 分數為 9.8/10，允許未經身份驗證的攻擊者上傳任意檔案，進而可能導致遠端程式碼執行（RCE）和網站完全被接管。實務影響極為嚴重，攻擊者可利用這些漏洞植入惡意程式碼。建議所有 Joomla 網站管理員應立即將受影響的擴充套件升級至最新版本，並同時檢查網站是否有未授權的帳號建立或可疑檔案上傳的跡象。",
    tags: ["Joomla", "CVE-2026-48908", "CVE-2026-56290", "SP Page Builder", "Page Builder CK", "遠端程式碼執行"],
    title_en: "Beware of Joomla Critical Vulnerabilities: SP Page Builder and Page Builder CK Exploited, Immediate Patching Recommended",
    summary_en: "Two critical vulnerabilities exist in the Joomla Content Management System extensions, and reports indicate they are currently being actively exploited. The affected vulnerabilities include CVE-2026-48908 (affecting the SP Page Builder extension, applicable to versions before Joomla 6.6.2) and CVE-2026-56290 (affecting the Page Builder CK extension, applicable to versions before Joomla 3.6.0). Both vulnerabilities have a CVSS v3.1 score of 9.8/10, allowing unauthenticated attackers to upload arbitrary files, which could subsequently lead to Remote Code Execution (RCE) and complete website takeover. The practical impact is extremely severe, as attackers can use these vulnerabilities to implant malicious code. All Joomla site administrators are advised to immediately upgrade the affected extensions to the latest version and simultaneously check the website for signs of unauthorized account creation or suspicious file uploads.",
    tags_en: ["Joomla", "CVE-2026-48908", "CVE-2026-56290", "SP Page Builder", "Page Builder CK", "Remote Code Execution"],
